---
description: empty null 
alwaysApply: false
---
  primaryAction?: {
    label: string
    onClick: () => void
  }
  secondaryAction?: {
    label: string
    onClick: () => void
  }
  helpAction?: {
    label: string
    onClick: () => void
  }
  className?: string
}

const EmptyState = ({
  variant,
  title,
  description,
  primaryAction,
  secondaryAction,
  helpAction,
  className
}: EmptyStateProps) => {
  const illustration = {
    "no-data": NoDataIllustration,
    "error": ErrorIllustration,
    "access-denied": AccessDeniedIllustration,
    "timeout": TimeoutIllustration,
    "not-found": NotFoundIllustration,
    "server-error": ServerErrorIllustration,
    "maintenance": MaintenanceIllustration
  }[variant]

  return (
    <div className={cn(
      "flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-6 text-center",
      className
    )}>
      {/* Illustration */}
      <div className="w-48 h-40 mb-4">
        {illustration}
      </div>

      {/* Content */}
      <div className="space-y-4 max-w-md">
        <h3 className="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">
          {title}
        </h3>
        <p className="text-sm text-gray-600">
          {description}
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* Actions */}
      <div className="mt-6 space-y-3">
        <div className="flex gap-2">
          {secondaryAction && (
            <Button
              variant="outline"
              className="bg-primary-lighter text-primary hover:bg-primary-lighter/80"
              onClick={secondaryAction.onClick}
            >
              {secondaryAction.label}
            </Button>
          )}
          {primaryAction && (
            <Button
              variant="default"
              className="bg-primary text-white hover:bg-primary/90"
              onClick={primaryAction.onClick}
            >
              {primaryAction.label}
            </Button>
          )}
        </div>
        {helpAction && (
          <Button
            variant="link"
            className="text-gray-700 hover:text-gray-900"
            onClick={helpAction.onClick}
          >
            {helpAction.label}
          </Button>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Usage Examples
```typescript
// No Data State
<EmptyState
  variant="no-data"
  title="No data available"
  description="There's no data to display at the moment. Try adjusting your filters or adding new data."
  primaryAction={{
    label: "Add Data",
    onClick: () => {}
  }}
  secondaryAction={{
    label: "Adjust Filters",
    onClick: () => {}
  }}
  helpAction={{
    label: "Learn how",
    onClick: () => {}
  }}
/>

// Error State
<EmptyState
  variant="error"
  title="Something went wrong"
  description="We encountered an error while processing your request. Please try again or contact support if the issue persists."
  primaryAction={{
    label: "Try Again",
    onClick: () => {}
  }}
  helpAction={{
    label: "Contact Support",
    onClick: () => {}
  }}
/>
```

### Usage Guidelines
1. Use for zero-state screens, error states, and no-results scenarios
2. Include clear, actionable titles and descriptions
3. Provide relevant primary and secondary actions
4. Use appropriate illustrations for different states
5. Maintain consistent spacing and alignment
6. Keep content concise and helpful
7. Include help or learn more links when needed

### Accessibility Considerations
- Use semantic heading structure
- Ensure proper focus management for actions
- Provide descriptive button labels
- Include ARIA labels where needed
- Support keyboard navigation
- Maintain sufficient color contrast

### Best Practices
1. Choose appropriate variant for the context
2. Write clear and helpful error messages
3. Provide actionable next steps
4. Use consistent illustration style
5. Implement proper loading states
6. Handle responsive layouts
7. Maintain consistent action placement

### Styling Guidelines
1. Use consistent spacing
2. Apply proper typography hierarchy
3. Implement clear visual hierarchy
4. Style buttons consistently
5. Handle illustration sizing
6. Maintain proper alignment
7. Consider mobile viewports